 "audio": "audio.mp3",
 "duration": 51.49,
 "text": "Want to switch careers? Don't start with a six-month course. Start with three conversations. A course costs months and money and you still won't know the most important thing. What's a normal Tuesday like in that job? So find three people who already do the work you want and ask them. Say you want to move into UX design. Search for UX designers. Look for alumni from your school or a friend of a friend. Send a short message. Hi, I'm thinking about moving into UX. Could I ask you three quick questions about your work? Keep the questions simple. What does a normal week look like? What do you wish you knew earlier? What should I learn first? Three conversations this week will tell you more than three months of guessing. Then pick the course if you still need one. That's what D-MUR is for. You archive your dream today so you can see it tomorrow and break it down into small steps you can actually do. If you want to try it out, I've put the link in the bio.",
